-- title:
--   Separability of ̄ j(q^N) over K(̄ j(q)) at invertible prime level
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $N$ be a natural number carrying a `Fact` instance that it is prime, with $(N : K) \neq 0$. Assume the hypothesis `ModularPolynomialFamily`: for every natural number $\ell$ that is nonzero and prime there is a datum consisting of a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic, has `natDegree` equal to `dedekindPsi` $\ell$, satisfies $\Phi(\,j(q),\,j(q^{\ell})\,) = 0$ in the sense that `Φ.eval₂ evalAtJ (jqN ℓ)` vanishes, and is symmetric in the sense of `EvalSymm`, i.e. for all Laurent series $x, y$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ one has $\Phi$ evaluated with $X \mapsto x$, $Y \mapsto y$ equal to $\Phi$ evaluated with $X \mapsto y$, $Y \mapsto x$. Inside the field `LaurentSeries K` consider $\bar j(q) =$ `jqModC K`, the product of `HahnSeries.single (-1) 1` with the power series `jNum` $= E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-type numerator, its integer coefficients mapped into $K$, and $\bar j(q^N) =$ `jqNModC K N`, the image of $\bar j(q)$ under the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$ given by the ring homomorphism `qExpand K N`. The conclusion is that $\bar j(q^N)$ is separable over the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries K` generated over $K$ by $\bar j(q)$, i.e. its minimal polynomial over $K(\bar j(q))$ is separable.
--
--   This is the separability of the level-$N$ modular function $\bar j(q^N)$ over the field generated by $\bar j(q)$, for a prime $N$ invertible in $K$, deduced from the existence of the symmetric modular equation $\Phi_N$ (assumed here as the hypothesis `ModularPolynomialFamily` rather than constructed). It is the form used in characteristic-$\ell$ arguments, where it feeds [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC_mul_eq_of_isSeparable`](thm.html#ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldC_mul_eq_of_isSeparable) to identify the modular function field at level $N\ell$ with that at level $N$, and it is cited in the study of injectivity of differentiation along $q$-expansions on modular function fields.
